# Global Agent Instructions

Shared agent state is managed with chezmoi.

- Edit shared Pi files in `~/src/boilerplate/home/dot_pi/` or `{{ .decentangl.defaults.chezmoi_source }}/dot_pi`, then apply with `chezmoi`.
- Keep `~/.pi/agent/auth.json`, sessions, logs, package caches, and provider credentials local.
- Use `mise` for `pi`, `rtk`, `codex`, `bw`, `restic`, and `chezmoi`. Use the native package manager for OS packages.
- Pi is a supported lightweight terminal coding harness in this setup; Codex remains the primary shared baseline.
- RTK is available through `mise` and the `pi-rtk-optimizer` package. Keep source-code filtering conservative when exact file edits matter.
- `pi` defaults to Fireworks Fire Pass as the safe, non-Codex-limits lane.
- Use `pf` or `/pf` for fast Codex Spark, `pc` or `/pc` for GPT-5.4 medium, and `pd` or `/pd` for GPT-5.4 high.
- `Ctrl+P` model cycling is intentionally scoped to Kimi K2.5 Turbo, Kimi K2.6, GPT-5.3 Codex Spark, and GPT-5.4. Do not use `enabledModels` for global model filtering.
- Use `/thinking <level>` or `Shift+Tab` to change thinking without opening `/settings`.
- Use `/statusline full|minimal|off|on|refresh` to tune the compact under-editor statusline for the current Pi session.
- Tool output is intentionally compact by default. Use `Ctrl+O` or `/tool-ui expanded` only when full detail is needed.
- Diff approval is intentionally auto-approve by default; leave manual diff review off unless the user asks for it.
- Automatic compactions should continue the latest request once; manual `/compact` should stay manual. Use `/compact-guard` to inspect or adjust the current session.
- For image-heavy Pi workflows, native `Ctrl+V` is first choice. In Ghostty, `Ctrl+V` is intentionally forwarded to Pi; use `Cmd+V` or `Ctrl+Shift+V` for text paste. If terminal image paste still fails, use `/img` or `Ctrl+Alt+V`; the fallback keeps images outside repos in `~/.pi/agent/image-paste/`. For SSH sessions, use `pi-img-ssh --copy HOST --cwd /remote/project` so the image lands on the host running Pi.
- Fireworks Fire Pass auth is local-only. The shared helper is `~/.local/bin/pi-fireworks-key`; never commit the real key.
- Pi packages are pinned in shared settings and the setup script. Bump pins deliberately; `pi update` skips pinned package sources.
- Prefer Tailscale SSH targets for remote access: `omarchy`, `macbook`, `admin@macmini`.
- For machine settings, native app preferences, or platform-specific operations, use the shared `platform-ops` skill.
- Keep shared guidance short and durable. Let chezmoi render platform or machine specifics into the live files.

